+The integrity modes are `ignore`, `repair`, and `fail`. `repair` removes broken or
+resolved entries and repairs safe misplaced files; `fail` rejects an inconsistent
+store without changing it.
+
 This can help in CI environments to prevent misconfiguration:
 For example, a CI build should probably never create a new the violation store, but operate on
 an existing one.
